{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a0a266850783fca7","name":"Aggressor-Series Battle Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-a0a266850783fca7","title":"Aggressor-Series Battle Droid","revision":15762,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:53:08Z","sha256":"7236100ea9188b1b96b6ae363b282240b636e4eade8b45bb70ec4f4c0822d182","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15762","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Aggressor-Series%20Battle%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a0a266850783fca7","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Built on the home planet of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Farghul"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farghul?action=edit&redlink=1"},", the Aggressor-Series Battle Droid is a cheap Droid designed for mass production and distribution. To the surprise of many other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Manufacturers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Manufacturers","referenceId":"reference:41c1bfb8b5b00c0a"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Farrfin Droidworks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farrfin_Droidworks?action=edit&redlink=1"}," has managed to produce large numbers of the Aggressor Droids despite Imperial restrictions on the creation of combat models. Unlike most Combat Droids, the Aggressor-Series Battle Droid does not come standard with any ranged weapons. In fact, most of its programming is dedicated to melee combat, making it an unusual, unorthodox, and unexpected opponent. As a result of this change in combat programming philosophy, the Empire has allowed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Farrfin Droidworks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farrfin_Droidworks?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to mass-produce and sell the Droids to other worlds, believing the Droids would be ineffective against the Empire's best marksmen.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In truth, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Farghul"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farghul?action=edit&redlink=1"}," designed the Aggressor Droids in response to the proliferation of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},"-wielding Sith in the galaxy. Though the Droids' primitive combat programming keeps them from being much of a threat to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Farrfin Droidworks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farrfin_Droidworks?action=edit&redlink=1"}," believes that the time will come when enough of its Droids are spread across the galaxy to challenge ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},", at which point an upgrade to the Droids' programming will turn them into a significant and widespread threat. The Droids' headpieces are modeled after ",{"tag":"a","children":["Farghul"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farghul?action=edit&redlink=1"}," war masks, though few in the Empire are so in tune with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Farghul"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farghul?action=edit&redlink=1"}," traditions to realize this bold statement in the Droids' design.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Krayt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Krayt","referenceId":"reference:c6d0b6bc88280f92"}," keeps several Aggressor-Series Battle Droids, using them as training Droids for his Sith underlings, including the training of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cade Skywalker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cade_Skywalker","referenceId":"reference:721cf41d59303a07"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Aggressor-Series Battle Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Aggressor-Series Battle Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +7; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 15, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 30, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 15\n"]},{"tag":